{
  "requirement": "The `Tsx` implementation of `OutlineLang` supplies the extension, selection, and fingerprint rules described in this chapter.\n\n```rust,ignore\npub struct Tsx;\n```\n\nTrait implementations\n\n```rust,ignore\nimpl Clone for Tsx;\nimpl Debug for Tsx;\nimpl Default for Tsx;\nimpl OutlineLang for Tsx;\nimpl Copy for Tsx;\n```",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "**Obligations in `requirements.sdk.sources.typescript.Tsx`:** (1) the public unit struct `Tsx`; (2) the trait implementations `Clone`, `Debug`, `Default`, `OutlineLang` and `Copy`; (3) `Tsx` supplies the extension, selection and fingerprint rules described in the chapter. Those detailed rules belong to the refining requirements (`...typescript.language`, `...fingerprints`, `...items`). Here I only check that `Tsx` is a working, correctly wired provider.\n\n**Coverage:**\n- `crates/trust-but-verify/tests/outline_content.rs#fn[bundled_languages_claim_extensions_and_supply_the_same_public_outline]` is marked `{test}` for this requirement. It runs the helper `check` with `languages::Tsx`, a `a.TSX` file, JSX source `function check() { return <div />; }`, selector `function[check]`, extensions `[\"tsx\"]` and scheme `tsx-structural-v1`. The helper `check` asserts:\n  - `extensions()` equals `[\"tsx\"]`, and `fingerprint_scheme()` equals `tsx-structural-v1`.\n  - `size_of::<L>() == 0`, `Clone::clone` works, and `L::default()` works. The bounds `L: OutlineLang + Default + Copy` make the compiler check the `Copy`, `Default` and `OutlineLang` impls. `OutlineLang: Clone` covers `Clone`.\n  - Inferring the language from an uppercase `.TSX` filename gives the same fingerprint and scheme as explicit `Tsx`. The root item span covers the whole source, the selector resolves, and `outline()` agrees with `from_source_with`.\n  - Structural search returns in-bounds ranges.\n- `typescript_and_tsx_share_signatures_abstract_classes_and_module_kinds` is also marked `{test}` for this requirement. It outlines the same source as `api.tsx` and `api.ts`. It asserts the exact selector list (generator and signature functions, abstract class and method, string-named and plain namespaces, and nested class and method) and that kinds are identical across both. That covers Tsx's selection rules.\n- `crates/trust-but-verify/tests/public_api.rs#fn[public_exports_match_the_appendix]` is marked `{test}` for the public API. Through `check_declaration` it compares the requirement's declared `Trait implementations` list (including `Debug` for `Tsx`) against the trait impls rustdoc reports. It also compares the declaration and exports. Any missing or extra impl, including `Debug`, would fail it.\n\n**Gaps:** None found. The `Debug` impl is checked only through the rustdoc inventory comparison, not by formatting a value. The requirement states no `Debug` output format, so that is enough. Obligations delegated to the refining requirements are not reassessed here. There are no acknowledgments.",
